\ A raise inside a word called from a quotation that a prelude combinator runs, pinned interpreted.
\
\ The `boom` row is the shape the header alone does not cover. Its frame is pushed while the
\ quotation's body is executing, so its source is the file the quotation was written in, not the
\ prelude file `choose` was defined in. `5 drop` keeps the call out of tail position, where the
\ frame would be elided.

boom: [ 1 "x" + ] ;

1 2 [ boom 5 drop ] choose
